<p>President Trump said Thursday he would remove tariffs and restrictions affecting Scotch whisky after King Charles III and Queen Camilla completed a four-day visit to the United States, calling the decision a gesture “in Honor of the King and Queen of the United Kingdom”. Trump said the move involved Scotland’s ability to work with Kentucky on whisky and bourbon, and cited wooden barrels used in the spirits trade as a reason people had sought the change for a long time. The Scotch industry and American distillers had lobbied the administration to eliminate a 10% tariff, arguing that the United States is the largest market for Scotch whisky and that Scottish distillers buy large numbers of oak barrels from Kentucky producers. Reports differed on the precise scope of the tariff relief, with some describing “certain” or “some” tariffs and others saying Trump promised to remove all tariffs and restrictions on whisky imports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/1zsZJuGfbvlBulEf05IHVTI0bnVsF9kHW8ueMkLsfbPUuelQHe6wwVH90OKLt5uxIHvBRdJIQ46zRSxsOHQlgHZGAbIo5qYbymfcSy4sqLkv7LBCvaLecSeNwhbTTysFQDdKK3YTWWFApx9COjVZSGyKfPznEjKZCkaFDrJy7FD1-o-Kb__-nsjZpr5kZi02-jADXNmw6BzVY_z28RIXrFKtcQ' alt='President Trump hosted King Charles III and Queen Camilla during their U.S. visit before announcing whisky tariff relief.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Trade hit: Shipments of Scottish whisky to the United States fell 15% between May and December 2025 after sweeping duties took effect in April 2025, according to figures from the Scottish Whisky Association cited by the New York Post.</li><li>Royal praise: Matichon said Trump called Charles “the greatest monarch” during the visit, while Newsis quoted Trump saying it had been a great honor to host the royal couple.</li><li>Diplomatic context: Politico said U.S.-UK relations had been strained since the start of the war with Iran, while AFP-cited coverage said the royal visit sought to repair ties after diplomatic disputes over the Middle East war.</li></ul><blockquote>The King and Queen got me to do something that nobody else was able to do, without hardly even asking! - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Buckingham Palace: The palace said the King expressed gratitude and would be “raising a dram” to Trump’s hospitality as he left the United States after the state visit. (<a href='https://www.irishnews.com/news/uk/trump-to-remove-scottish-whisky-tariffs-after-king-and-queens-us-visit-672SLSHLSFKLTCC7JREB7FZP74/'>Irish News</a>)</li><li>Scottish First Minister John Swinney: Swinney said he had just returned from U.S. meetings to press for a better Scotch deal; Newsis reported that he said the tariff had been costing Scotland’s economy millions of pounds each month. (<a href='https://www.irishnews.com/news/uk/trump-to-remove-scottish-whisky-tariffs-after-king-and-queens-us-visit-672SLSHLSFKLTCC7JREB7FZP74/'>Irish News</a>, <a href='https://www.newsis.com/view/NISX20260501_0003614412'>Newsis</a>)</li><li>U.S. trade authorities: U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer described the move as preferential tariff treatment for UK-produced whisky; Matichon said the administration had not answered whether that meant elimination or reduction. (<a href='https://www.matichon.co.th/foreign/news_5700176'>Matichon</a>)</li><li>Scotch industry officials: Industry officials called the tariff deal a “significant boost” for the sector, The Guardian reported. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/30/trump-tariffs-whisky-imports'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-lifts-tariffs-on-scotch-whisky-in-nod-to-king-charles/a-77007503'>Trump lifts tariffs on Scotch whisky in nod to King Charles</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3352087/trump-says-hes-lifting-some-tariffs-scotch-whisky-after-king-charles-visit'>Trump says he’s lifting some tariffs on Scotch whisky afte